[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2945990655","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107180#issuecomment-2945990655","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107180","id":2945990655,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vmD__","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-05T20:04:26Z","updated_at":"2025-06-05T20:35:59Z","body":"I can't reproduce this on 4.5.dev5 (Linux + NVIDIA):\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dfa94cea-f755-4d77-b166-d4ed3f4053ba)\n\n[The Celeron N3060 is an Atom Braswell CPU](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/products/sku/91832/intel-celeron-processor-n3060-2m-cache-up-to-2-48-ghz/specifications.html). I don't know if these have full Vulkan support on Windows. On Linux, you may be getting limited Vulkan support as part of Mesa, but it's not a conformant implementation. In fact, you'll probably see a warning message every time you run a Vulkan app from a terminal (try installing and running `vkcube`).\n\nRemember that when you're using Compatibility, you still need Vulkan support to bake lightmaps.\n\nAnother possibility is that you're running out of RAM, especially on a system with only 4 GB of RAM and integrated graphics (which means the graphics have to share with the system). This is being tracked in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/95204.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2945990655/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2946092877","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107180#issuecomment-2946092877","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107180","id":2946092877,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vmc9N","user":{"login":"ianilychh1","id":130171767,"node_id":"U_kgDOB8JDdw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/130171767?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ianilychh1","html_url":"https://github.com/ianilychh1","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ianilychh1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ianilychh1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ianilychh1/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ianilychh1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ianilychh1/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ianilychh1/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ianilychh1/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ianilychh1/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ianilychh1/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-05T20:27:46Z","updated_at":"2025-06-05T20:27:46Z","body":"The official drivers for Windows 10 definitely don't have Vulkan drivers.","author_